1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:03,124
One narrow strait carries about
a fifth of the world's oil.

2
00:00:03,209 --> 00:00:04,119
What if it closed?

3
00:00:04,315 --> 00:00:08,355
The Strait of Hormuz is about 33
kilometres wide at its narrowest,

4
00:00:08,355 --> 00:00:09,725
between Iran and Oman.

5
00:00:10,005 --> 00:00:13,485
About a fifth of the world's oil,
and a large share of its liquefied gas,

6
00:00:13,485 --> 00:00:14,961
sails through it.

7
00:00:14,961 --> 00:00:17,611
India imports most of
the crude oil it uses,

8
00:00:17,901 --> 00:00:19,911
and a big part of that
comes from the Gulf.

9
00:00:20,071 --> 00:00:22,821
Close the strait and prices
would jump within hours.

10
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:27,557
India keeps emergency stocks, but they
cover only about ten days of demand.

11
00:00:27,742 --> 00:00:31,292
It could buy more from Russia,
West Africa and the United States,

12
00:00:31,542 --> 00:00:34,372
but every alternative takes
longer and costs more.

13
00:00:34,422 --> 00:00:38,302
Saudi Arabia and the UAE have
pipelines that bypass the strait,

14
00:00:38,302 --> 00:00:39,898
but not enough to replace it.

15
00:00:39,898 --> 00:00:41,728
Who would suffer most if Hormuz closed?

16
00:00:41,973 --> 00:00:42,603
Comment.

